# The qiniu Kodo credentials and endpoints every call in this directory signs
# with. It lives here rather than next to the Auth record that carries it
# because it is this module's configuration: qiniu/sign, qiniu/rs and
# qiniu/stats all take one, and none of them needs anything else from svc.

## Qiniu Kodo config for fm signing.
##
## `rs_host` / `up_host` are the management and upload endpoints qiniu/rs talks
## to. They are configuration rather than constants for one reason: it is the
## only seam at which a contract run can hold the object-store paths (COPY of a
## subtree, PUT, DELETE of an object) to a golden without a live bucket — point
## them, and QINIU_DOMAIN, at a local fake. main.dawn defaults them to the real
## qiniu hosts, so an unconfigured deployment is byte-identical to before; no
## code below this line knows whether it is talking to a fake.
pub type Qiniu = { ak: String, sk: String, bucket: String, domain: String, expires: Int, rs_host: String, up_host: String }
